Gegenprobe: Abmelden bei gesperrtem Gerät scheitert, weil der neue Ablageschlüssel nicht entstehen kann
Modul: core-security
Test: ch.brickinventoryapp.security.StoreUnlockedTest
Rot: sign-out with a locked device deletes the old key, the new one exists only when unlocked

diff --git a/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/StoreKey.kt b/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/StoreKey.kt
--- a/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/StoreKey.kt
+++ b/Android-App/core-security/src/main/java/ch/brickinventoryapp/security/StoreKey.kt
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@
         state++
         // Locked, the new one is only created on the next access: a sign-out in the background
         // should not fail just because the device isn't letting anything be encrypted right now.
-        catchUnlessCancelled { fetch() }
+        fetch()
     }
 
     /** Derived with HMAC-SHA256: database and files don't share a key. */
